    "summary": "Added src/workflow/__tests__/gate-guarded-entry-points.test.ts: a table of 15 guarded entry points (handleStart/Plan/Step/Synthesize, runWorkflowServerSide, runStart, handleImplement, handleStandaloneImplement, handleValidate, handleStandaloneValidate, approveArtifactByJsonPath, approveWorkflowTarget, resolveReviewFinding, the daemon review's handleVerdicts and reviewArtifactFile), each with the gate call it must make and a minimum count (synthesize and the workflow driver need two: the recheck before writing). The test reads each function with the TypeScript AST and counts call expressions inside its body (nested closures included, which covers approveWorkflowTarget's refuseBeforeRecord), so deleting a call fails it; I confirmed that by removing the synthesize recheck, which failed with 'must call assertMayAuthor at least 2 time(s); it calls it 1', then restored the file. It also checks that any file in the workflow-step and build-step phases dirs that calls a gate function is listed, and that analyze-step, code-review-step, analyze-oneshot, analyze-rpc and code-review-rpc neither import the team gate modules nor call a gate function and are not on the inventory. Added a test with the exact title 'the terminal approve and resolve commands print the refusal naming the holder, formatted beside the review-block message' to gate-refusal-output.test.ts: approve, resolve, and (via the real team services with injected gate deps) claim and release print cross-prefixed lines naming the holder, beside the review-block line.",
